# {{name}}

{{description}}

A Sophon model provider plugin that connects to the {{Name}} LLM API
for text generation and chat completions.

## Implemented Interface

`IModelProvider` from `Sophon.Plugin.Abstractions`

### Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `HealthCheckAsync` | Checks if the {{Name}} API is reachable |
| `CompleteAsync` | Sends a chat completion request and returns the response |
| `StreamCompleteAsync` | Streams completion chunks (SSE) |
| `GetCapabilities` | Returns model capabilities (vision, tools, context window) |

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- .NET 10 SDK
- `Sophon.Plugin.Abstractions` NuGet package
- A {{Name}} API key

### Build

```bash
dotnet build
```

### Configuration

When adding this provider in the Sophon Dashboard (Settings > Models), configure:

| Setting | Type | Required | Description |
|---------|------|----------|-------------|
| `apiKey` | Secret | Yes | API key for {{Name}} |
| `endpoint` | String | No | Base URL (default: `https://api.example.com/v1`) |
| `defaultModel` | String | No | Default model ID |

### Install

```bash
sophon plugins install ./{{Name}}.dll
```

## Development Guide

1. Update the API endpoint and authentication in the constructor
2. Implement `CompleteAsync` with your provider's request/response format
3. Implement `StreamCompleteAsync` if the provider supports SSE streaming
4. Update `GetCapabilities` with accurate model information
5. Test the health check, completion, and streaming flows

## Supported Models

| Model ID | Context Window | Vision | Function Calling | Streaming |
|----------|---------------|--------|-----------------|-----------|
| `default` | 8,192 | No | Yes | Yes |

